    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "Punch — Stay With Me",
      "content": "Giving reasons. \"Because I love you, I'll stay.\"\n\nStay With Me is the central theme from the 2016-2017 drama Goblin (도깨비, also known as Guardian: The Lonely and Great God), performed by Punch with Chanyeol of EXO. The drama follows an immortal goblin cursed to live for centuries until he finds his human bride, and the song plays during the show's most fated, aching romantic moments — the pull between two people who feel connected across lifetimes, and the sorrow of a love that's shadowed by eventual, inevitable separation.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-아/어서**, which means \"because / and then.\" We'll see how Punch uses it in \"Stay With Me.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **보다** — to see\n- **듣다** — to hear\n- **좋아해서** — because I like (you)\n- **보고 싶어서** — because I miss (you)\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
